sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 (a task group is one root task; Pi turns use the pi driver), Recall swamp-tasks-swamp-orchestrates-pi + task-vms-swamp-via-ssh, DECISIONS R1-R4.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rule 22. Cut 2026-11-02 (orchestrator): provision creates the VM and the workspace only; the group-run driver composes tasks.check, tasks.turn, tasks.publish, tasks.park and tasks.cancel.
  %% Reviewed: Nick 2026-11-03 (P1): the workspace gets the Project's Route and Processes through the same children as instance:create; rules 23 and 25. What it covers, capacity and image fallback are on the docs page.
  %% status: reviewed
  %% command: tasks:provision
  %% kind: tasks.provision
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane VM icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane H icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant VM as Task VM<br/>tvm-88 over ssh
  participant H as Incus host<br/>Node 14 · VM power
  CLI->>GW: tasks:provision 42
  Note over GW: Validate, record the task<br/>group 42: reserved · task #5140
  %%> When it waits:
  %%> - no host has room or a usable image: the task waits (`capacity`) and starts when a VM is destroyed or an image is promoted
  opt Project serves a web root and task_workspace_routed is on
    Note over GW: Reserve the Route<br/>task-42.blog.test · private
    %%> Why first:
    %%> - the Route changes how Process units render; capturing Processes after it keeps admission and dispatch identical
  end
  opt Project has Process definitions
    Note over GW: Capture the Processes<br/>dev definitions
  end
  GW->>SW: Push the VM secrets<br/>vault: model key, Pi token
  %%> Why:
  %%> - secrets go Gateway → vault → step; the run inputs hold only vault key names
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-task-provision
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task #5140
  SW->>H: Create and prepare the VM<br/>launch · WireGuard · Pi server
  SW->>VM: Set up the workspace<br/>clone · Project setup steps
  %%> Why redacted:
  %%> - setup output stays on the VM; only a redacted 4 KiB tail reaches history
  opt the task declares a topology
    SW->>VM: Start the nested fleet<br/>task-nested-fleet child
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - creates the nested network from the subnet that the ready copies of the seed store, copies the three ready copies, gives each its stored MAC and address, and starts them
    %%> - joins as operator: the VM makes its own WireGuard key, writes the public key into the nested Gateway's operator record with `incus exec`, puts it on the hub and brings up `wg-nested` as 10.45.0.10
    %%> - pushes the proof Swamp Club key from the VM into the nested Gateway and restarts its Swamp
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the task owns the network and the three VMs; it needs no earlier fleet and no state from another VM (stage 2 of the command development pipeline)
    %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review: a seed without its three ready copies skips the fleet until the fleet build (`task_vm.fleet_build`) lands; the result records `nested_fleet: none`
    %%> Not built yet in this step:
    %%> - the NFS mount of the checkout, the apply step, the readiness check and the `base` snapshot
  end
  opt the workspace has a Route or Processes
    Note over SW: Bind the workspace keys<br/>pin the guest host key
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the guest's host key exists only after the VM step pins it; the Gateway leaves only the guest's targets unpinned
  end
  opt Project serves a web root and task_workspace_routed is on
    SW->>VM: Route the workspace<br/>operation-route-create child
    %%> Why a child:
    %%> - the same Route child instance:create runs; its signing authorizes against this root run
  end
  opt Project has Process definitions
    SW->>VM: Create, start Processes<br/>operation-process-create · forEach
  end
  Note over SW: Check the workspace<br/>receipt · VM, source, base
  Note over SW: Accept the workspace<br/>fails on an error_code
  alt every step passes
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Record result<br/>group 42 running · VM 88 ready
  else a step fails
    VM--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or timeout
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark the task failed<br/>group asks for help
    %%> On the VM:
    %%> - VM 88 and its checkout stay; there is no rollback; `tasks:cancel 42` ends the group and removes the VM
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show #5140
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
